Contributors
------------

None yet besides the maintainer. If you have had a change merged, add yourself
here in the same commit — this file is the authoritative credits list, and the
person best placed to spell your name correctly is you.


Contact
-------

Bugs and feature requests
  https://github.com/vikas-kumawatt/Gossips/issues

Security vulnerabilities — never a public issue
  https://github.com/vikas-kumawatt/Gossips/security/advisories/new

No personal email address is published here on purpose. The channels above are
tracked, searchable, and do not become a spam target; a mailbox in a public
repository is all three of the opposite.


A note on copyright
-------------------

Contributors retain copyright over what they write; there is no CLA and no
copyright assignment. That is the ordinary arrangement for an AGPL project and
it has one consequence worth stating plainly: once code from another author is
merged, the project can no longer be relicensed or dual-licensed commercially
without every such author's agreement. Until that happens, the maintainer holds
the entire copyright and retains both options.
